specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:551:**Commit frames are not emitted in index order.** Above, `entry_commit` for index 1 arrives after `entry_upsert` for index 2. A thinking entry is committed when the next text segment arrives, not when a tool entry appears, so a tool call between thinking and the answer lands in the gap. A client that assumes commits arrive in ascending index order, or that an entry is committed before the next one opens, will mis-render this exchange ([validated by: commits the thinking entry when text resumes, not when a tool entry appears](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L175)).
