specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:8:Every `user_message` the server receives now ends in exactly one `stream_end`, whatever happens in between, so a client has a single, un-raced signal that a run is over. Before this change a failed run ended with an `error` frame and no `stream_end`, while the protocol told clients to treat either frame as terminal; that rule could not be followed, because an unrelated `error` (a malformed `ping`) can arrive between two `entry_delta` frames of a healthy run and would read as the run ending early.
